{
  "introduction": [
    {
      "Section": "Title",
      "Description": "Sounds, Symbols, and Spellings of Tiv Words"
    },
    {
      "Section": "Overview",
      "Description": "Tiv sounds in general have nasal sounds. However, there are flat sounds: consonant sounds, vowel sounds, and consonant-vowel sounds."
    },
    {
      "Section": "Vowel Sounds",
      "Description": "Vowel sounds are made by allowing the breath to come out freely as the lips are pursed."
    },
    {
      "Section": "Consonant Sounds",
      "Description": "To make a consonant, the breath stream is partly blocked, and the sound lowered or raised."
    },
    {
      "Section": "Note",
      "Description": "A word as it is spelled may have different meanings depending on the way it is pronounced."
    }
  ],
